ch hands coated with radium paint under ultraviolet light","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARadium_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/WWI_German_altimeter_radium_painted.jpg/500px-WWI_German_altimeter_radium_painted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/WWI_German_altimeter_radium_painted.jpg/1280px-WWI_German_altimeter_radium_painted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/WWI_German_altimeter_radium_painted.jpg/500px-WWI_German_altimeter_radium_painted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A zeppelin altimeter from World War I. The dial, previously painted with a luminescent radium paint, has turned yellow due to the degradation of the fluorescent zinc sulfide medium.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWWI_German_altimeter_radium_painted.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Radior_cosmetics_containing_radium_1918.jpg/500px-Radior_cosmetics_containing_radium_1918.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Radior_cosmetics_containing_radium_1918.jpg/500px-Radior_cosmetics_containing_radium_1918.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1918 ad for Radior, one of several cosmetic products claiming to contain radium for its purported curative properties[58]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARadior_cosmetics_containing_radium_1918.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Pam%C3%A1tn%C3%ADk_objevu_radia_v_J%C3%A1chymov%C4%9B.jpg/500px-Pam%C3%A1tn%C3%ADk_objevu_radia_v_J%C3%A1chymov%C4%9B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=t